  "published": "2026-09-17T10:34:28.973Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Every asynchronous read and write now has an overload taking a CancellationToken, threaded through to the underlying TextReader and TextWriter: ReadAsync, SkipAsync and GetSchemaAsync on the readers, WriteAsync, WriteSchemaAsync and WriteRawAsync on the writers, the typed readers and writers, ReadAllAsync and WriteAllAsync, and the type mappers' ReadAsync and WriteAsync. The overloads without a token are unchanged for callers and are now default interface members that forward CancellationToken.None, so a class outside the library implementing IReader, IWriter, ITypedReader, ITypedWriter or a type mapper interface adds the token overloads. Source-compatible with 7.1.0 for callers.",
